          "filename": "A memorial to coalminers. Greymouth, New Zealand . (16469132551).jpg",
          "caption": "Traditional mining was highly dangerous. There were three main causes of accidents: rock falls, often when the pillars were mined; explosions, most frequently occasioned by firedamp (methane gas given off by coal), which was usually ignited by a miner’s naked flame; and tubs travelling on the haulage system knocking men over.",
